weak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skidzTweak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-30T22:26:01Z","updated_at":"2013-12-30T22:34:57Z","body":"kk, did some more digging.. I don't really know much about openid and such, so a little confused to how it all should work.. but.. this is what I found... \n\nWhen calling fetchAttrubutes() function in OpenId.php... the collection its looping through ($this->data) doesn't have any of the attributes its looking for, and that's why it fails the authentication and gives the #400 error... \n\nExample of keys in my $this->data:\nstring(1) \"r\" -\nstring(10) \"authclient\"\nstring(9) \"openid_ns\"\nstring(11) \"openid_mode\"\nstring(18) \"openid_op_endpoint\"\nstring(21) \"openid_response_nonce\"\nstring(16) \"openid_return_to\"\nstring(19) \"openid_assoc_handle\"\nstring(13) \"openid_signed\"\nstring(10) \"openid_sig\"\nstring(15) \"openid_identity\"\nstring(17) \"openid_claimed_id\"\n\nnone of them start with \"openid_sreg_\" (fetchSregAttributes searchs for) and \"openid_ns\" has no alias (fetchAxAttributes looks for it)...\n\nLet me know if  you need anymore info.. I personally don't know enough about openid to fix any of this. \n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/31372874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"